  "prefLabel": "Nur 805.02 Ancillary Instructors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 805.02 Ancillary Instructors. Both the medication nurse-reviewer and a medication skills instructor shall have the authority to appoint a person with expertise in one or more of the program's curriculum topics to teach one or more courses or hours of the theoretical component of the curriculum if such expert's instruction is:\n\n(a) Within the area of expertise; and\n\n(b) Under the supervision of a medication skills instructor.\n\nSource. #7742, eff 8-13-02; ss by #8873, eff 4-24-07 (formerly Nur 906.02); ss by #10303, eff 3-22-13; ss by #10572, eff 4-17-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nur100-800.html"
